content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-111 — AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-21100",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Vibration: the reported 4.2 mm/s falls within Figure 3 Zone B, 2.8–4.5 mm/s RMS, described as suitable for long-term operation. It is below the 4.5 mm/s RMS boundary for Zone C, “Restricted - plan maintenance,” and below the 7.1 mm/s RMS boundary for Zone D, “Damage likely - stop the pump.” Figure 3 is the applicable bearing-housing vibration-velocity limit; the report must be confirmed as an RMS housing measurement, and readings from both housings are needed so the highest can be classified.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Temperature: 74°C exceeds the documented normal bearing-housing limit of up to 70°C by 4°C, but remains 6°C below the 80°C alarm and 16°C below the 90°C trip. These limits apply to temperature measured on the bearing-housing surface; 74°C is therefore above normal but is not, by itself, an alarm or trip reading.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Non-drive-end grinding noise: there is no numeric noise threshold, but the bearing-replacement rule explicitly applies when either bearing shows wear, noise or high temperature. The reported noise and above-normal housing temperature therefore trigger replacement of both bearings as a pair even though the vibration reading remains in Zone B.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal condition: “seal is dry” has no documented numeric limit and is ambiguous. A dry exterior would not, by itself, match the troubleshooting symptom “leakage at shaft seal.” If it instead means operation without seal flush, the applicable requirement is Plan 11 flush from pump discharge and “never run dry”; that meaning must be clarified before further operation.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Non-drive-end bearing wear or damage is the leading suspected cause because it best fits the localised grinding noise and above-normal temperature. Bearing wear is a documented cause of high bearing temperature, and noise or high temperature requires replacement of the bearing pair.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Over-greasing is a possible contributor to the above-normal bearing temperature. The troubleshooting table directs the technician to check grease quantity; the report provides no grease-quantity evidence.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment is another documented cause of high bearing temperature and high vibration. Record the as-found condition where practicable and perform laser alignment after any work that moves the motor or bearing housing.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Impeller imbalance or damage and cavitation/NPSH problems are lower-priority alternatives to exclude if the bearing, grease and alignment findings do not explain the symptoms. They are documented possible causes of high vibration, not confirmed findings on this pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Before further operation, clarify whether “seal is dry” means no visible external leakage or actual dry running. Verify Plan 11 flush from pump discharge; do not run the pump dry. If dry running or a seal defect is confirmed, re-scope the work to include the applicable seal troubleshooting and replacement procedure.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Confirm and record vibration velocity in mm/s RMS on both bearing housings and classify the highest value using Figure 3. Record bearing-housing surface temperatures and identify the housing and location for each reading.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For back pull-out or seal disassembly, isolate and drain the pump. During inspection, check grease quantity and examine the bearings and impeller; check alignment and NPSH as needed to distinguish bearing wear, over-greasing, misalignment, impeller damage/imbalance and cavitation.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Replace both bearings as a pair: one HF3-510 non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3 and one HF3-512 drive-end bearing 6312-C3. Do not replace only the noisy non-drive-end bearing.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the casing is opened, install a new HF3-120 casing gasket. Do not add mechanical-seal replacement solely on the basis of a dry exterior. If seal replacement is separately confirmed, follow procedure 5.2: remove the back pull-out assembly and impeller, withdraw the seal and sleeve, inspect the sleeve for scoring, and fit the new seal and a new casing gasket.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "On reassembly, use Table 5 torques with lightly oiled threads: bearing-housing bolts M12 to 85 Nm; impeller nut M24 to 160 Nm if removed; casing bolts M16 to 210 Nm if disturbed. If seal work is added, fit HF3-450 for this serial and tighten its M10 seal-gland nuts to 25 Nm, not the service bulletin’s 30 Nm.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After any work that moves the motor or bearing housing, perform laser shaft alignment to a maximum parallel offset of 0.05 mm and angular tolerance of 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After repair, record the housing-surface temperatures and vibration on both bearing housings. Resume the documented weekly vibration monitoring, classify the highest reading using Figure 3, and investigate any recurrence of noise or temperature above the normal 70°C limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3; item 6. Replace as part of the matched bearing-pair scope.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3; item 5. Replace together with the non-drive-end bearing.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket; item 8. Have one available and replace it whenever the casing is opened.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Current vibration and temperature do not reach the documented stop/trip limits: vibration is below Zone D and temperature is below both alarm and trip. However, Figure 3 identifies Zone D, shown from 7.1 mm/s RMS, as “Damage likely - stop the pump”; the temperature limits remain alarm at 80°C and trip at 90°C.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Never operate the pump with a dry-running mechanical seal. Seal flush is Plan 11 from pump discharge; loss of flush must be resolved rather than treating the current vibration Zone B as permission to run dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For the documented back pull-out/seal procedure, isolate and drain the pump before removing the assembly. The back pull-out design allows removal of the rotating assembly without disturbing the casing or pipework.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg and lifting equipment is required whenever that assembly is removed.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Bearing replacement, pair: standard labour allowance 6.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: allow 1.5 hours with 1 technician when the work moves the motor or bearing housing; apply the documented alignment tolerances after that work.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical-seal replacement is excluded from the base labour scope pending clarification of “seal is dry.” If seal replacement is confirmed and added, its standard allowance is 4.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "The manual parts list and Table 5 support component seal HF3-450 and 25 Nm seal-gland nuts, while SB-2026-014 prohibits HF3-450 and requires cartridge seal HF3-450B at 30 Nm. The bulletin, issued 14 March 2026, applies only to HF-300 pumps serial HF3-22000 and above. P-111 is HF3-21100, below that range, so the bulletin does not apply: if seal work is required, retain HF3-450, use manual Table 5 and 25 Nm, and inspect the sleeve under procedure 5.2. The bulletin’s HF3-450B, 30 Nm torque, pre-set-seal instruction and 0.1 mm scoring criterion are not applied to this asset.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Is the reported 4.2 mm/s an RMS velocity measured on a bearing housing, which housing was measured, and what was the reading on the other housing? The manual requires both housings to be measured and the highest reading classified. (C06, C07)",
    "Was 74°C measured on both bearing-housing surfaces or only at the non-drive end, and what measurement location was used? The documented limits apply to housing-surface temperature. (C01, C02)",
    "Does “seal is dry” mean no visible leakage, or that the seal has operated without Plan 11 flush? If dry running is meant, do not continue operation and determine whether seal damage and seal-replacement scope exist. (C02, C09, C10)",
    "The evidence does not provide a step-by-step bearing-replacement procedure, grease type or required grease quantity, or confirmation of which casing, impeller and seal components must be disturbed for bearing access. Confirm the approved disassembly method before finalising gasket, seal and fastener scope. (C05, C09, C10, C11)",
    "If the shaft sleeve is inspected during added seal work, the manual provides no numeric scoring rejection limit for this pre-bulletin serial. Do not assume the bulletin’s 0.1 mm criterion applies without engineering direction. (C10, C13)",
    "No P1/P2/P3 response-time matrix or required completion date is supplied. P2 is a planning judgement based on bearing noise and above-normal temperature, not an OEM-defined priority; the required repair date remains to be confirmed. (C02, C07, C10)"
  ]
}
